# Main-family certificate data, kernel-friendly encoding

Same certificate data as the emitter's `adder_cert_main.json`, re-encoded
kernel-friendly (the KB frozen-table pattern): `omega` and `live` are packed
64 states per `Nat` chunk (base 8 / base 2), chunks in a two-level 36×32
list, so a random access costs ~70 kernel steps and one small GMP `pow`
(exponent < 64, under the kernel exponentiation threshold); `rho` and
`forced` stay as small assoc tables.  `main_cert_ok_kernel` is proved by
`decide +kernel` (~4 min, no compiler axiom) — the kernel-tier swap the
brief's endgame asked for.
